Track 1: Iron Anne Swallows the Annealing Flame
- Story & Context: In the valley town of Val d'Elsa, master glass-blower Anne Keller collapsed after attempting to capture a 70-beat-per-minute respiratory rhythm inside a hand-blown lead flask, an accident that sparked the band's first jam session inside the monastery walls. The studio session nearly ended when the valve amps caught fire, but the resulting take caught the exact moment the local church bells melted in the 1998 foundry fire. Connects directly to the monastery’s dream-patches via an interpolated sub-bass drone mapped from Keller’s hospital telemetry. Vane belts out the track's defining moment: "Breathe the hot lead down until the choir turns to salt!"
